614 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 306 0 R
/E (Robotics and Artificial Intelligence are no longer confined to laboratories or theoretical explorations; they are increasingly becoming integral to how we perceive, interact with, and shape the physical world. As we move towards an era of intelligent and autonomous systems, the real challenge lies not merely in developing smarter algorithms, but in translating intelligence into meaningful actions, reliable systems, and impactful solutions. I believe the future of intelligent systems will be shaped by our ability to integrate mechanical intelligence, computational methods, data-driven learning, and human-centric design, and to prepare young researchers to develop technologies that are intelligent, accessible, responsible, and relevant to societal needs.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
