694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 311 0 R
/E (Robots are evolving from executing predefined routines to perceiving, learning, and adapting to changing environments. This talk explores that transition through manipulation and locomotion intelligence, highlighting how reinforcement learning, vision-language-action models and world models work alongside planning and control. It examines the scale, diversity and quality of data needed to generalize across tasks and environments. Equally important are robot hardware, actuators, sensors, and batteries, which determine physical capability, perception and endurance. Drawing on industrial robotics, the talk discusses how intelligence, data, and hardware must advance together to enable adaptable, reliable autonomy.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<<
