<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Intelligence Through Interaction: Sensing, Learning, and Control for Robotic Manipulation)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
723 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
724 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Robots that open a jammed bottle lid or snap-fit a spectacle lens into its frame need far more than precise motion; they need a kind of intelligence that senses, perceives and learns through real-world interaction. This talk explores how physical interaction can be designed to understand and complete manipulation tasks, drawing on recent work from our lab: coordinating a delicate assembly, dismantling an unfamiliar mechanism, and combining vision and contact control to wipe multi-panel surfaces. These examples expose a basic challenge: the same action can lead to different outcomes in the real world, making sensing and learning from physical interactions crucial for robot skills that respond to uncertainty in contact-rich manipulation.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
725 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (ABOUT THE SPEAKER)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Prof. Harish J. Palanthandalam-Madapusi received his B.E. from SPCE, University of Mumbai, and his M.S.E. and PhD from the University of Michigan in 2007. He was an Assistant Professor at Syracuse University until 2011, when he joined IIT Gandhinagar, where he has held several leadership roles, including Dean \(Campus Development\), Dean \(Student Affairs\) and Dean \(General Administration\). He has authored more than 90 journal and proceedings papers and led over twenty research and consulting projects with agencies such as ISRO and the Indian Navy and with industry partners. He is co-founder of AB6 Robotics, and his research focuses on robotics and robot control, particularly manipulation.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
