740 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 314 0 R
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
741 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 314 0 R
/E (Industry 5.0 emphasizes human-centric, sustainable and resilient manufacturing by integrating intelligent automation with human expertise. In this context, mobile manipulators, which combine the mobility of robotic platforms with the dexterity of robotic arms, offer significant potential for flexible and adaptive manufacturing systems, performing material handling, machine tending, assembly, inspection and intralogistics across dynamic environments. Integrating artificial intelligence, machine vision, force sensing and intelligent motion planning lets them operate autonomously while collaborating safely with human workers. The talk explores the enabling technologies, emerging applications and key challenges in deploying mobile manipulators for intelligent manufacturing.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
742 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 314 0 R
/E (ABOUT THE SPEAKER)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
743 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 314 0 R
/E (Prof. Santhakumar Mohan is a Professor in the Department of Mechanical Engineering and Head of the Centre for Robotics and Control at IIT Palakkad. He received his PhD in Robotics and Control from IIT Madras in 2010 and has held visiting positions at IISc Bangalore, KAIST, RWTH Aachen, ECN France and BSTU Russia. His honours include the Outstanding Young Scientist Award from the Korea Robotics Society and the Alexander von Humboldt Fellowship. He has published more than 150 research papers, holds 13 granted Indian patents, and has served as Technical Editor of IEEE/ASME Transactions on Mechatronics and Associate Editor of IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters. He is the founding Director of IPTIF, IIT Palakkad TRIP and TECHIN.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
