805 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 318 0 R
/E (Efficient coverage path planning is essential for mobile robots operating in complex real-world environments, where missions demand a delicate balance among competing performance metrics such as energy consumption, turning frequency, and elevation constraints. This talk explores advanced multi-objective evolutionary frameworks designed to generate optimal Pareto fronts, moving beyond single-metric approaches to provide robust, adaptable navigation strategies. It shows how integrating these optimization methods translates into substantial efficiency gains and smoother physical execution for autonomous mobile robotic systems.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
806 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 318 0 R
/E (ABOUT THE SPEAKER)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
807 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 318 0 R
/E (Prof. Hari Kumar Voruganti is a Professor in the Department of Mechanical Engineering at the National Institute of Technology Warangal \(NITW\), and holds a PhD from IIT Kanpur. His research focuses on multi-DOF robot kinematics, redundancy resolution, and collision-free path planning in complex workspaces. He actively explores optimization-driven methodologies for high-performance automation and robotic navigation. His recent work addresses coverage path planning of mobile robots in uneven terrains.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
