/P 319 0 R
/E (From Demonstrations to Deployment: Integrating AI, Control and Hardware in Wheeled Humanoids)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
820 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
821 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (Wheeled humanoids bring mobile manipulation to environments designed for people, but the full potential of a learned policy depends on a well-integrated system. This talk examines that integration challenge through the development and deployment of wheeled humanoid systems. Following a representative manipulation task, it traces the path from teleoperation and data collection through imitation and reinforcement learning to execution on hardware. It explores how actuator integration, kinematics, motion planning, compliant control, simulation, calibration, and fault handling make learned behavior physically feasible, responsive and repeatable, and concludes with practical considerations for safe physical interaction, consistent behavior across robots, and systematic evaluation.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
822 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (ABOUT THE SPEAKER)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
823 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 319 0 R
/E (Dr. Anubhav Dogra is a Senior Autonomy Engineer in Controls & AI at Humanoid in London, UK. He has a background in mechanical engineering, a PhD in robotics from IIT Ropar and postdoctoral research experience at the University of Warwick, UK. His work focuses on integrating software with physical hardware, bridging learned AI policies and control systems in wheeled and bipedal humanoids. His work spans robot bring-up, actuator and sensor integration, whole-body kinematics and dynamics, simulation development, and controllers that ensure safe, repeatable physical interaction in industrial deployments.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
