837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (Autonomous robotics is rapidly moving beyond isolated machines toward intelligent systems that can perceive, decide, navigate, and act in real-world environments. This talk explores the common intelligence stack behind both autonomous ground vehicles and aerial robotic systems, examining how AI, computer vision, LiDAR, sensor fusion, localization, path planning and control come together to enable safe and adaptive autonomy. Using ground and aerial mobility as complementary examples, it also discusses the transition from simulation to physical systems, the role of edge AI and real-time decision-making, and research opportunities in robotics, AI, multi-agent systems, and Physical AI.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
838 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (ABOUT THE SPEAKER)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
839 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 320 0 R
/E (Mr. Muralikrishnan E is the Head of Edutech Future Mobility Labs at Edutech India Pvt. Ltd., where he leads initiatives in autonomous mobility, ADAS, electric vehicles, software-defined vehicles and intelligent robotic systems. His interests include autonomous ground and aerial platforms, sensor fusion, perception, localization, path planning, control, ROS 2/Autoware, and Physical AI. He works closely with academic institutions, research organizations and industry to develop future-mobility laboratories, research platforms, and training programs. He holds an M.S. in Telecommunications Engineering from Victoria University, Melbourne, and a B.E. in Electronics and Communication Engineering from the University of Madras.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
