/E (Progress in robot learning is increasingly limited by data rather than model architecture. This session walks through the full data supply chain for physical AI: capturing egocentric multi-modal video in working factories, consent and privacy handling, quality control, multi-layer annotation \(hands, objects, actions, language\), dataset formats for training, and the move from human video to robot policies via retargeting and teleoperation. Drawing on field deployments across Punjab manufacturing units, it shows what works, what breaks, and where open research problems remain, such as embodiment gap, label noise, and evaluation. Attendees will see each stage visually and leave with a practical checklist for designing their own robot-data pipelines.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
869 0 obj
<<
